I used to worry about rings of polymorph, until I accidently (sure,
sure) put one on.  I exploded out of my body armour in a shop and I
didn't have enough money to pay for the ring.  Even when I changed into
a newt or even a blob, I couldn't take my ring off (yes, stuck to my
foreclaw / scale)!  I thought it was all over.

After a cup of coffee, I calmed down, waited until I turned into a
powerful vampire lord, and I killed the shopkeeper.  I ran / slithered
/ slimed / flew to Gnome town but I couldn't find a can of grease.
ICK!  Later, I found a nymph, dropped everything, and I got the ring
stolen.

The fun part with being two score different monsters one after another
was it was hard to die!  I carried my speed boots, helmet, shield of
reflection, and weapon.  If I became a small monster, I waited until I
changed into something big before picking my stuff up and continuing.
If I was killed while being a monster, I became human again.

This character later ascended with 9166234 points,

